WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.158
- Good morning, Believe Nation,

00:00:01.158 --> 00:00:04.229
my name is Evan Carmichael,
my one word is Believe

00:00:04.229 --> 00:00:05.849
and I believe that entrepreneurs

00:00:05.849 --> 00:00:08.965
are going to solve all of
the world's major problems.

00:00:08.965 --> 00:00:10.448
So to help you on your journey today,

00:00:10.448 --> 00:00:14.494
we're going to learn how you
can focus on the right people.

00:00:14.494 --> 00:00:16.704
Over to you, Trevor Noah.

00:00:16.704 --> 00:00:18.745
(rooster crowing)

00:00:18.745 --> 00:00:21.461
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:21.461 --> 00:00:24.096
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:00:24.096 --> 00:00:27.196
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:27.196 --> 00:00:29.221
- Well, you have to find the
people, that are for you,

00:00:29.221 --> 00:00:31.310
you have to understand whenever
you're creating a product,

00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:33.118
whether it's music, whether
it's comedy, whether it's TV,

00:00:33.118 --> 00:00:34.782
you're not trying to make it for everyone,

00:00:34.782 --> 00:00:35.631
you're trying to find the people,

00:00:35.631 --> 00:00:37.219
that you're trying to make it for.

00:00:37.219 --> 00:00:38.542
You've got to stick to your truth

00:00:38.542 --> 00:00:40.296
and then you find those
people and you believe in it,

00:00:40.296 --> 00:00:41.630
so you go, "Is it good?"

00:00:41.630 --> 00:00:43.089
and then I understand, I go,

00:00:43.089 --> 00:00:45.045
"So, your lady and her Mom are watching?"

00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:47.024
and then even if you're hating on me,

00:00:47.024 --> 00:00:48.444
then I go, "Fine, then it's not for you,"

00:00:48.444 --> 00:00:49.895
I know you're not--
- Fuck that guy, that guy.

00:00:49.895 --> 00:00:51.594
- but I go, "Yeah, you're
not, but I have to focus

00:00:51.594 --> 00:00:53.477
"on the people who are
watching me 10 times

00:00:53.477 --> 00:00:56.055
"and I'm going to keep on
building on those people."

00:00:56.055 --> 00:00:58.965
So at the end of the day,
if you focus on the people,

00:00:58.965 --> 00:01:00.098
that are trying to block you,

00:01:00.098 --> 00:01:02.053
you don't spend enough
time enjoying the people,

00:01:02.053 --> 00:01:03.310
that are celebrating you.
- That's right.

00:01:03.310 --> 00:01:04.731
If you want to have success,

00:01:04.731 --> 00:01:07.432
then you need to pay careful
attention to the environment,

00:01:07.432 --> 00:01:09.123
that you have around for yourself.

00:01:09.123 --> 00:01:10.055
If you are surrounded by people,

00:01:10.055 --> 00:01:12.287
who are telling you that you can't do it,

00:01:12.287 --> 00:01:14.009
that you suck, that it's
never going to work,

00:01:14.009 --> 00:01:16.234
that you don't have the
skills or the education

00:01:16.234 --> 00:01:18.114
or the money or whatever reason,

00:01:18.114 --> 00:01:19.914
you will never be a success,

00:01:19.914 --> 00:01:22.109
because of all these
logical, practical things.

00:01:22.109 --> 00:01:23.392
If you're surrounded by those people,

00:01:23.392 --> 00:01:25.359
then guess what happens?

00:01:25.359 --> 00:01:26.765
Nothing happens.

00:01:26.765 --> 00:01:28.065
You don't go off and do the big thing,

00:01:28.065 --> 00:01:30.468
because you're constantly
surrounded by negativity.

00:01:30.468 --> 00:01:32.440
It's why so many people just

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:34.709
are the average of their
five friends, right,

00:01:34.709 --> 00:01:36.100
so look at who your five friends are

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:38.158
and do you want to be like that or not?

00:01:38.158 --> 00:01:39.378
Now, it doesn't mean that you

00:01:39.378 --> 00:01:40.629
have to completely cut them off,

00:01:40.629 --> 00:01:42.338
it doesn't mean that you need to,

00:01:42.338 --> 00:01:44.291
you know, shun your family,

00:01:44.291 --> 00:01:45.635
but you need to start creating

00:01:45.635 --> 00:01:48.231
a more supportive
environment for yourself.

00:01:48.231 --> 00:01:49.962
You may be saying, "But Evan, I don't know

00:01:49.962 --> 00:01:51.008
"any more successful people,

00:01:51.008 --> 00:01:52.832
"I don't know how to break free,

00:01:52.832 --> 00:01:53.665
"I'm in a crappy area

00:01:53.665 --> 00:01:55.832
"and everybody around
me tells me that I suck

00:01:55.832 --> 00:01:58.333
"and I don't know who
else to go and turn to."

00:01:58.333 --> 00:02:00.104
This is the first of your many challenges,

00:02:00.104 --> 00:02:02.583
that you will come across
as an entrepreneur.

00:02:02.583 --> 00:02:05.833
It's always going to be about
creatively solving problems.

00:02:05.833 --> 00:02:07.463
It's about how resourceful you can be,

00:02:07.463 --> 00:02:09.639
instead of how many resources you have.

00:02:09.639 --> 00:02:10.617
So here's the first challenge,

00:02:10.617 --> 00:02:12.249
"I don't know any successful people,

00:02:12.249 --> 00:02:14.083
"what am I going to go out and do?

00:02:14.083 --> 00:02:16.394
"Who am I going to turn to for advice?"

00:02:16.394 --> 00:02:18.450
The first person I turned to to advise

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:20.350
in my business was my banker.

00:02:20.350 --> 00:02:23.081
I didn't know anybody,
I had no connections,

00:02:23.081 --> 00:02:24.351
nobody in my family was an entrepreneur,

00:02:24.351 --> 00:02:25.501
I didn't know who to talk to,

00:02:25.501 --> 00:02:28.412
so I went to my banker and I said,

00:02:28.412 --> 00:02:31.551
"Hi, I'm Evan, I have a
business bank account with you.

00:02:31.551 --> 00:02:32.957
"I'd love to know how you might be able

00:02:32.957 --> 00:02:33.790
"to help my business.

00:02:33.790 --> 00:02:36.247
"Any ideas you have would be fantastic."

00:02:36.247 --> 00:02:37.850
He said, "Well, do you need a loan

00:02:37.850 --> 00:02:40.357
"or do you need financing?"

00:02:40.357 --> 00:02:43.455
I was like, "I dunno,
maybe, I don't know,"

00:02:43.455 --> 00:02:44.964
"I'm trying to figure it out.

00:02:44.964 --> 00:02:45.797
"I'm just starting,

00:02:45.797 --> 00:02:47.736
"trying to figure out what
I'm doing with my company,

00:02:47.736 --> 00:02:49.304
"I'd love your advice and input."

00:02:49.304 --> 00:02:52.184
He's like, "Well, that's
not what we do, as a bank.

00:02:52.184 --> 00:02:54.474
"You know, we give out loans."

00:02:54.474 --> 00:02:55.786
I thought banks were, you know,

00:02:55.786 --> 00:02:57.447
the friends of entrepreneurs.

00:02:57.447 --> 00:02:59.420
So this is how naive I was, right

00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:01.522
and this is how little knowledge I had

00:03:01.522 --> 00:03:02.922
and how few connections I had,

00:03:02.922 --> 00:03:05.910
that I went to my banker, you know,

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:08.069
but one conversation leads
to another conversation

00:03:08.069 --> 00:03:10.845
leads to another conversation
and another conversation.

00:03:10.845 --> 00:03:12.762
You're not going to get
the supportive environment

00:03:12.762 --> 00:03:14.045
by just sitting on your couch, right,

00:03:14.045 --> 00:03:16.203
you've got to go out and
start talking to people

00:03:16.203 --> 00:03:18.883
and connecting and
understanding, asking for help.

00:03:18.883 --> 00:03:21.141
People love to help,

00:03:21.141 --> 00:03:23.476
but the risk is you're
not going to do any work.

00:03:23.476 --> 00:03:26.804
If you come to me and you ask me for help,

00:03:26.804 --> 00:03:28.239
I'm jaded, because of all the people,

00:03:28.239 --> 00:03:29.947
who've asked me for help
and I gave them advice,

00:03:29.947 --> 00:03:31.948
that they did nothing with.

00:03:31.948 --> 00:03:34.484
So you're immediately
lumped in with those people.

00:03:34.484 --> 00:03:37.578
So what you want to do is ask
for just a tiny bit of time.

00:03:37.578 --> 00:03:39.111
Ask for one little bit of advice

00:03:39.111 --> 00:03:40.635
and promise and show your hustle,

00:03:40.635 --> 00:03:42.880
promise that you're going
to do the work on it

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:45.705
and then when you get
the advice, do the work

00:03:45.705 --> 00:03:48.196
and then come back and say,
"Listen, I took that advice."

00:03:48.196 --> 00:03:49.398
Don't go and ask for a mentor.

00:03:49.398 --> 00:03:52.211
They don't want to commit
to a relationship with you.

00:03:52.211 --> 00:03:54.951
One bit of advice, I
used two fingers there,

00:03:54.951 --> 00:03:58.223
one bit of advice
(laughs), one on each hand,

00:03:58.223 --> 00:03:59.937
and then go and do the work and come back

00:03:59.937 --> 00:04:03.095
and say, "Listen, I did
this work and it worked!"

00:04:03.095 --> 00:04:05.407
or, "didn't work, I tried, I
did hours and hours and hours

00:04:05.407 --> 00:04:06.362
"and it didn't work out.

00:04:06.362 --> 00:04:07.638
"How do I make it better?"

00:04:07.638 --> 00:04:09.790
If they see that you're
taking the initiative

00:04:09.790 --> 00:04:13.955
and actually executing, now
you're starting to ascend up.

00:04:13.955 --> 00:04:15.882
There's other ways to be
surrounded by people though too,

00:04:15.882 --> 00:04:19.911
it's not just mentorship,
join a Meet Up group,

00:04:19.911 --> 00:04:21.604
connect with online communities,

00:04:21.604 --> 00:04:23.899
we have an awesome online
community here on Believe Nation,

00:04:23.899 --> 00:04:25.414
where people are supporting each other

00:04:25.414 --> 00:04:27.787
and try to help each
other with their business,

00:04:27.787 --> 00:04:31.262
join other online groups,
learn from virtual mentors.

00:04:31.262 --> 00:04:34.833
One of the things that helped me the most

00:04:34.833 --> 00:04:37.026
and me thinking bigger

00:04:37.026 --> 00:04:38.819
and wanted to play on a different level

00:04:38.819 --> 00:04:40.908
and thinking I could do
more and really feeling

00:04:40.908 --> 00:04:42.812
like I could have a big
impact on this world,

00:04:42.812 --> 00:04:45.649
one of the things, that helped me most

00:04:45.649 --> 00:04:48.639
was my own YouTube channel.

00:04:48.639 --> 00:04:51.281
It's selfish for me that
I'm sharing it with you,

00:04:51.281 --> 00:04:54.487
it's a selfish endeavor for
me, that I share with you guys

00:04:54.487 --> 00:04:58.869
and I'm so grateful and so
happy, that you enjoy it too.

00:04:58.869 --> 00:05:00.970
When I'm around constantly
Elon Musk and Steve Jobs

00:05:00.970 --> 00:05:02.704
and Oprah Winfrey and all these people,

00:05:02.704 --> 00:05:04.097
who have done amazing things

00:05:04.097 --> 00:05:06.170
and are still pushing to try to be better,

00:05:06.170 --> 00:05:08.725
when I'm in that environment,

00:05:08.725 --> 00:05:12.617
I want to do bigger things, I
want to have a much bigger impact.

00:05:12.617 --> 00:05:15.783
So the more I'm around that,
the more it shifts my focus,

00:05:15.783 --> 00:05:17.176
it shifts my attention

00:05:17.176 --> 00:05:20.665
and makes me feel like
I can contribute more

00:05:20.665 --> 00:05:23.228
and it builds a new
environment for myself.

00:05:23.228 --> 00:05:25.097
If you want to do great things,

00:05:25.097 --> 00:05:28.394
you need to create an
environment of greatness,

00:05:28.394 --> 00:05:30.400
otherwise it's never going to work.

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:33.066
So the question today is, I'm curious,

00:05:33.066 --> 00:05:35.684
what kind of people do
you have in your life

00:05:35.684 --> 00:05:37.305
and are they the right people to help you

00:05:37.305 --> 00:05:39.050
get to where you need to go.

00:05:39.050 --> 00:05:40.263
What changes are you going to make,

00:05:40.263 --> 00:05:41.627
after watching this video?

00:05:41.627 --> 00:05:43.537
I'm curious, leave it down
in the Comments below,

00:05:43.537 --> 00:05:44.824
I'm super curious to find out.

00:05:44.824 --> 00:05:47.591
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Dave Gardner

00:05:47.591 --> 00:05:49.248
from thedavegardner.com.

00:05:49.248 --> 00:05:51.570
Dave, thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:05:51.570 --> 00:05:54.189
Your One Word, doing a
review, taking a picture,

00:05:54.189 --> 00:05:55.798
I really, really appreciate it, man

00:05:55.798 --> 00:05:57.592
and I'm so glad that you enjoyed the book.

00:05:57.592 --> 00:05:59.577
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:05:59.577 --> 00:06:02.525
I believe in you, I hope you
continue to believe in yourself

00:06:02.525 --> 00:06:05.370
and whatever Your One Word is, much love

00:06:05.370 --> 00:06:07.003
and I'll see you again tomorrow morning

00:06:07.003 --> 00:06:10.173
for another shot of espresso.

00:06:10.173 --> 00:06:12.578
♫ I wake up every morning

00:06:12.578 --> 00:06:16.327
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:06:16.327 --> 00:06:18.054
(typewriter keys clicking)

00:06:18.054 --> 00:06:19.496
- You're happy with it though?

00:06:19.496 --> 00:06:20.603
- I'm real happy with it.
- Yeah, yeah.

00:06:20.603 --> 00:06:22.851
- When I see this thing play
in front of an audience,

00:06:22.851 --> 00:06:23.830
people go crazy.

00:06:23.830 --> 00:06:24.663
- Oh yeah.

00:06:24.663 --> 00:06:26.102
What's your, what is one of those

00:06:26.102 --> 00:06:28.648
Inside the Actors Studio for us,

00:06:28.648 --> 00:06:31.601
like so what's your
process, once you do this,

00:06:31.601 --> 00:06:33.519
you want to watch it with
all the audience here,

00:06:33.519 --> 00:06:35.469
you don't want to see it, you study this,

00:06:35.469 --> 00:06:36.910
what's your process, once you,

00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:38.539
once they say, "Cut! That's a wrap."

00:06:38.539 --> 00:06:39.565
- You know what, you cut it up, you know,

00:06:39.565 --> 00:06:40.986
you've got to watch it with an audience,

00:06:40.986 --> 00:06:42.478
it's not drama.
- Right.

00:06:42.478 --> 00:06:45.935
- Drama is whatever you want it to be.

00:06:45.935 --> 00:06:49.063
When you make drama, you are like Picasso

00:06:49.063 --> 00:06:51.600
you're just like, "OK, whatever."

00:06:51.600 --> 00:06:54.813
When you make comedy, you're
not that kind of painter,

00:06:54.813 --> 00:06:57.049
you're like a painter
down at the promenade,

00:06:57.049 --> 00:06:58.210
painting portraits of people,

00:06:58.210 --> 00:06:59.043
you know what I'm saying,

00:06:59.043 --> 00:07:00.379
"Oh, you want more blue in your eyes?

00:07:00.379 --> 00:07:01.748
"I'm going to put more blue in your eyes.

00:07:01.748 --> 00:07:03.067
(laughing)

00:07:03.067 --> 00:07:04.173
"You want to be taller?

00:07:04.173 --> 00:07:05.694
"Okay, you're taller."

00:07:05.694 --> 00:07:07.215
You know, I'm one of those guys.

00:07:07.215 --> 00:07:08.048
- Right.

00:07:08.048 --> 00:07:08.881
- So that's, when you make comedy,

00:07:08.881 --> 00:07:10.846
you make it for the
people and I, you know,

00:07:10.846 --> 00:07:15.195
you try to have as many
screenings and as many tests

00:07:15.195 --> 00:07:17.715
and you do focus groups
and you read the card,

00:07:17.715 --> 00:07:19.176
so you try to give the
people what they want

00:07:19.176 --> 00:07:21.047
and that's comedy, man.
- Yeah.

00:07:21.047 --> 00:07:21.880
- People ask me from time to time,

00:07:21.880 --> 00:07:24.064
"Do you make a movie with
an audience in mind?"

00:07:24.064 --> 00:07:24.897
- [Interviewer] Yeah.

00:07:24.897 --> 00:07:25.985
- and my answer is, "Yes, I do."

00:07:25.985 --> 00:07:27.575
alright, but the audience I have in mind

00:07:27.575 --> 00:07:29.921
isn't some faceless blobs, that
I'm trying to second guess,

00:07:29.921 --> 00:07:31.163
(laughs) alright,
- Yeah.

00:07:31.163 --> 00:07:31.996
- It's me.

00:07:31.996 --> 00:07:32.829
- [Interviewer] You
sound like a focus group.

00:07:32.829 --> 00:07:34.342
- Yeah, it's me, I'm the audience,

00:07:34.342 --> 00:07:36.692
I'm the guy that goes out
and pays seven dollars

00:07:36.692 --> 00:07:38.298
or eight dollars in New York, (laughs)

00:07:38.298 --> 00:07:40.713
you know, to go and see a movie, alright.

00:07:40.713 --> 00:07:42.374
I go so, if I'm excited
about seeing a movie,

00:07:42.374 --> 00:07:44.142
I see it on opening day, alright,

00:07:44.142 --> 00:07:47.402
I am the audience, alright,
and I know what I want to see,

00:07:47.402 --> 00:07:49.986
you know, and I was betting

00:07:49.986 --> 00:07:52.797
and I was a little surprised
at how many there were,

00:07:52.797 --> 00:07:54.638
I was betting that there were other people

00:07:54.638 --> 00:07:56.611
like me out there, alright.

00:07:56.611 --> 00:07:58.664
Now true, I'm making specific films

00:07:58.664 --> 00:07:59.802
and if you make a specific film,

00:07:59.802 --> 00:08:00.872
that's not everything for everybody,

00:08:00.872 --> 00:08:02.334
you're going to turn
some people off, alright,

00:08:02.334 --> 00:08:04.781
but you're going to
turn some people on too.

00:08:04.781 --> 00:08:08.316
- In the old day, when I
start the action movies,

00:08:08.316 --> 00:08:10.219
I just make audience laughing, you know,

00:08:10.219 --> 00:08:13.322
do all the funny things, you
know, ah, like, ohh, like this

00:08:13.322 --> 00:08:16.148
and kick their ball in
(audience laughing).

00:08:16.148 --> 00:08:17.591
So that's a?
- It is really, yeah.

00:08:17.591 --> 00:08:19.040
- Oh, really?
- Yeah, yeah.

00:08:19.040 --> 00:08:22.179
- You know, but slowly,
slowly, from the audience,

00:08:22.179 --> 00:08:24.850
from the audience,
(laughs) from the media,

00:08:24.850 --> 00:08:25.683
- [Interviewer] Yeah.

00:08:25.683 --> 00:08:27.628
- Especially from the fans,
they write the letter,

00:08:27.628 --> 00:08:30.871
"Oh, now I have a baby, so
sad I cannot see the movie,

00:08:30.871 --> 00:08:33.865
"because the dirty word, but
because the dirty action,

00:08:33.865 --> 00:08:35.775
"because this,"

00:08:35.775 --> 00:08:39.813
all those years, I change,
change, change, change, change,

00:08:39.813 --> 00:08:41.693
but without all the dirty things,

00:08:41.693 --> 00:08:44.830
still can make the audience
laughing, that's the difficult.

00:08:44.830 --> 00:08:47.286
It's the audience, all
the fans, all the media,

00:08:47.286 --> 00:08:50.038
teach me becoming a good filmmaker.

